Pick dates, and the game pauses when each one arrives. Useful for stepping away during a long stretch at speed 5, or for stopping right before a truce ends, a pregnancy comes due or an activity finishes.

[h2]How to use[/h2]
[list]
[*] Click the [b]clock icon[/b] left of the date in the bottom bar.
[*] Pick a date with the Year / Month / Day buttons, or add to it with the quick buttons (+1w, +1m, +3m, +6m, +1y, +5y, +10y).
[*] Optionally choose a [b]Reason[/b] from 36 presets (Truce ends, Pregnancy due, Siege, Council task, Save the game, ...).
[*] Click [b]Set stop[/b].
[/list]
Up to 6 stops are listed with their reasons, and the ✕ beside one removes it. [b]Clear all[/b] removes everything. When a date arrives the game pauses and a popup lists the reasons.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*] Crusader Kings III 1.20
[*] Safe to add to an existing save
[*] Replaces no vanilla files, so it works alongside UI mods
[*] Stops follow you when you switch characters
[*] English only. Other languages show English.
[/list]

Also available for Victoria 3: [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3827384545]Date Stop[/url].

[h2]Source[/h2]
Source code and issue tracker: [url=https://github.com/keanfreeman/ck3-date-stop]github.com/keanfreeman/ck3-date-stop[/url]

